                      %mrow
                        %mi COSHEP
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} COSHEP
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"}> Todd Trimble
                \: created
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PRO"} PRO
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cube+category"} cube category
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/TAC/volumes/11/8/11-08.pdf"} paper
                on cubical sites. Discussion with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"} David Corfield
                at
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+set"} cubical set
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \: added the example of “derived schemes with
                = succeed "-ring\u201D-valued" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+scheme"} generalized scheme
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"} Zoran Škoda
                separated Lurie material, with a link from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme+as+locally+affine+structured+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} scheme as locally affine structured (infinity,1)-topos
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \: thanks, Zoran. I have renamed the entry to say
                = succeed "-topos," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \: added the alternative definition in terms of sheaves on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Aff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff/X
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                expanded the definition at
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
              %p
                added a word on the definition of morphisms, gave the sheaf-theoretic version and the definition from the derived scheme perspective. In that context I cited the full paragraph of Jacob Lurie where he argues that the standard definition is misleading in that it asserts an underlying topological space, and that one better thinks of a scheme as having an underlying
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-topos"} 0-topos
              %ul
                %li
                  Urs why not separating this into another entry like scheme over a locale. There is zillion of things which should still enter into the entry of scheme and people needing basic info on schemes do not want hi-tech things which have no advantage in usual geometry, but rather as a motivation for generalizations ? Moreover this reinterpretation is missing the point of relative point of view. One usually have schemes over
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                    \: sure, let’s split off sub-entries when it gets too long. You are currently locking the entry, otherwise I would have done it.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"} Zoran Škoda
                changes to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+scheme"} generalized scheme
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %ul
